          "summary": "Add ownership section: Company owns Content, Site deliverables and Site customer data; HDI keeps its platform but licenses embedded IP; no joint ownership.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] The Agreement is silent on intellectual property, so we have added an ownership section confirming that we own our Content, the Site deliverables developed for us and all customer and order data collected through the Site, with HDI retaining its pre-existing platform and tools and granting us a perpetual, royalty-free licence to anything of its own embedded in the deliverables. We can accept a licence-back approach to the Site deliverables instead of assignment if HDI prefers, provided our ownership of Content and customer data is unqualified.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0035",
              "numbering": "5.5",
              "text": "5.5 Ownership of Content, Deliverables and Data. (a) As between the Parties, the Company owns and shall retain all right, title and interest in and to the Content, the Marks, all materials relating to the Deerskin Products, and all designs, text, graphics, layout, look and feel and other deliverables and work product created or developed by or for HDI specifically for the Company or the Site under this Agreement (collectively, the \"Company Materials\"), and HDI hereby assigns to the Company all right, title and interest it may have in and to the Company Materials. (b) HDI retains all right, title and interest in and to its pre-existing computer systems, hosting platform, software, Content administration tools and general know-how, and hereby grants the Company a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free, transferable license to use, reproduce, modify and sublicense any such HDI materials to the extent incorporated in, or reasonably necessary to use, the Company Materials or the Site. (c) All customer, user, order and transaction data, including customer e-mail lists, collected through the Site or otherwise in connection with Deerskin Products shall be the exclusive property of the Company; HDI may use such data solely as necessary to perform its obligations under this Agreement and shall, upon the Company's request and upon expiration or termination of this Agreement, deliver a copy of such data to the Company in a commercially reasonable format. (d) Nothing in this Agreement shall create any joint ownership of intellectual property, and neither Party acquires any right in the other Party's intellectual property except as expressly granted in this Agreement."
            }
